                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The game is quite fun (a simplified XCOM with a cool setting). However, my understanding is that this game got review bombed by a lot of Turkish players (no disrespect to any nationality).\n\nSupposedly (and I could be wrong), a Turkish player had an account banned for either a forum or discord server for Heart of Iron IV (an unrelated game, mind you). As part of an appeal process, some issue occurred with said player having used the image of Mustafa Kemal Atatürk, that this was somehow linked with their ban, and that apparently some double standard had been committed. Of note, Atatürk is a highly controversial figure connected to genocides (i.e the Greek/Pontic genocides), and that a central claim was that using his photo was permissible because other people also used highly controversial figures for their account but didn't get banned. \n\nGrievances aside, a game should be judged by its merits, and this game is quite fun. A bit odd that this has to be explained.",
